      "note": "Created as a SECOND `Logbook`; v4's `docMountPoints.create` runs `nextUniqueMountPointName`, so it lands as `Logbook (2)`. That is the point: v4 cannot hold two stores with the same trimmed lower-cased name, because `repairMountPointNameCollisions` — keyed on the IDENTICAL `name.trim().toLowerCase()` as `collectAmbiguousStoreNames` — runs at the doc-mount-points lazy table init, i.e. inside the very `findEnabled()` the search calls. The store-name AMBIGUITY arm is therefore unreachable through the route on either side; it is pinned at unit tier (`ref_for_mount_arms`). The RESERVED-name arm (`self`) is untouched by the repair and IS exercised here."
